  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1210 AM CDT Thu Sep 24 2026\n\nMinimal change is expected in the overall pattern through the next \nseveral days as a mid-level ridge continues to influence the South \nTexas region. Adequate moisture in the area combined with daytime \nheating, will allow for up to a 50-65% chance for isolated to \nscattered showers and thunderstorms Thursday afternoon primarily \nacross the southern Brush Country. Otherwise, mainly dry conditions \nare expected through the weekend, with only a low chance for \nisolated showers into early next week associated with the sea breeze.\n\nAbove-normal temperatures will continue through the period across \nthe region. Afternoon heat index values will generally range between \n100-109 degrees, while overnight lows remain quite warm in the mid \nto high 70's. These conditions will prevail through the weekend and \ninto early next week.\n\nGlancing ahead to the middle of next week, guidance continues to \nindicate the potential for a possible disturbance to approach or \nmove across the area. However, notable differences remain among the \nmodels regarding its evolution, timing, and potential impacts. Given \nthe continued uncertainty this far out, will refrain from making any \nsignificant changes to the forecast until better agreement\nemerges.",
